A SECOND close candidate is fatal in BOTH frames: 0.1% / 0.7% clear at
n_close == 2 against 66.6% / 81.0% at n_close == 1, and 0.0% above that.
That is the tie and margin policy acting as a veto, not a property of
either population. 31.8% of the production frame sits in that dead zone
against 22.6% of the benchmark, which is where the composition points are.

