11:       D2-prefix      0.0       0.0

A1-name-zip5 is the strongest key there is -- exact name plus ZIP5. The
benchmark clears half its identities on it; the production frame under a
third, leaning on token-level matching instead. That follows from how the
frame is drawn: address groups carrying two or more DISTINCT recipient
names select for names that do not render consistently, so the exact-name
keys that carry the benchmark are the keys that fail here.

